blic inputs are validated. Explicit random bytes and buffer offsets make tests and boundary integrations deterministic without changing the generator's default monotonic state."},"183":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","type":"page","content":"Choosing an ID","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id"},"184":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","content":"Choose for the system boundary, not the trend."},"185":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id#a-good-default","content":"A good default"},"186":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id#time-ordering-is-local","content":"Time ordering is local"},"187":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id#time-order-leaks-creation-time","content":"Time order leaks creation time"},"188":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","content":"Different identifiers optimize for different constraints. Start with the boundary the value crosses: database index, URL, public API, MongoDB collection, or a native integer column."},"189":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","content":"Situation"},"190":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","content":"Choose"},"191":{"id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides